 <body class="guide-body stories-page studio-site" data-page="podaturpet-stories-and-culture">
-  <a class="pt-skip" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><header class="pt-site-header" data-pt-shared="header"><!-- PT:shared:header:START --><div class="pt-header-inner"><a class="pt-brand" href="/" aria-label="Podaturpet home"><img src="/images/podaturpet-emblem.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44"><strong>PODATURPET</strong></a><nav class="pt-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/lungi-product-catalogue.html">Lungi Catalogue</a><a href="/podaturpet-town-guide.html">Explore Podaturpet</a><a href="/podaturpet-local-business-directory.html">Local Directory</a><a href="/#contact">Contact</a></nav></div><!-- PT:shared:header:END --></header><section class="guide-hero stories-hero studio-town-hero"><div class="guide-shell studio-town-hero-grid"><div class="studio-town-copy"><div class="guide-kicker">PODATURPET / VILLAGES / CULTURE</div><h1>Podaturpet, and the places that make its story.</h1><p class="guide-lead">Follow the threads from a weaving town to its village neighbourhoods, festival streets and the hills of the wider region.</p></div><figure class="studio-image"><img src="/images/powerloom-video-poster.jpg" alt="A powerloom from the supplied weaving video" width="848" height="478" decoding="async" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The craft behind the cloth · From our weaving footage.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
+  <a class="pt-skip" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a><header class="pt-site-header" data-pt-shared="header"><!-- PT:shared:header:START --><div class="pt-header-inner"><a class="pt-brand" href="/" aria-label="Podaturpet home"><img src="/images/podaturpet-emblem.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44"><strong>PODATURPET</strong></a><nav class="pt-nav" aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/lungi-product-catalogue.html">Lungi Catalogue</a><a href="/podaturpet-town-guide.html">Explore Podaturpet</a><a href="/podaturpet-local-business-directory.html">Local Directory</a><a href="/#contact">Contact</a></nav></div><!-- PT:shared:header:END --></header><div class="mr-top-credit" lang="en"><img src="/images/muraraj-mr-logo.svg" alt="" width="32" height="32" decoding="async"><span>Developed &amp; Maintained by <strong>MuraRaj Technologies</strong></span></div><section class="guide-hero stories-hero studio-town-hero"><div class="guide-shell studio-town-hero-grid"><div class="studio-town-copy"><div class="guide-kicker">PODATURPET / VILLAGES / CULTURE</div><h1>Podaturpet, and the places that make its story.</h1><p class="guide-lead">Follow the threads from a weaving town to its village neighbourhoods, festival streets and the hills of the wider region.</p></div><figure class="studio-image"><img src="/images/powerloom-video-poster.jpg" alt="A powerloom from the supplied weaving video" width="848" height="478" decoding="async" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The craft behind the cloth · From our weaving footage.</figcaption></figure></div></section>
   <main class="guide-main" id="main-content"><div class="guide-shell"><nav class="guide-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/podaturpet-town-guide.html">Town guide</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Podaturpet Stories and Culture</span></nav>
 <div class="stories-reading"><nav class="story-jumps" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#town-story">Town &amp; weaving</a><a href="#village-directory">Village directory</a><a href="#festival-story">Festivals</a><a href="#regional-stories">Around the region</a><a href="#story-sources">Sources</a></nav><article class="guide-story studio-story" id="town-story"><h2>A place of looms, fields and everyday enterprise</h2><p>Podaturpet’s own civic profile brings two livelihoods into the same picture: weaving and agriculture. It describes handloom work, powerlooms linked to homes, and paddy cultivation. The town’s textile identity belongs within that wider working landscape.</p><p>The profile traces the Town Panchayat to 1939. That date marks civic administration; it does not establish when people first settled here. For a visitor, the most rewarding starting point is the relationship between cloth, work and the town around it.</p><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://townpanchayat.in/podhaturpet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Podhaturpet Town Panchayat: general profile ↗</a></p></article><section class="pt-feature pt-split" id="weaving-in-motion"><div><div class="pt-kicker">THE CRAFT BEHIND THE CLOTH</div><h2>See the loom at work.</h2><p>Watch the weaving footage from our collection, then follow the making of a checked lungi from yarn selection to finishing.</p><a class="pt-button" href="/how-checked-lungis-are-made.html">Follow the weaving process</a></div><figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/images/powerloom-video-poster.jpg" aria-label="Powerloom weaving footage"><source src="/images/Powerloom.mp4" type="video/mp4"><a href="/images/Powerloom.mp4">Watch the weaving video</a></source></video><figcaption>Weaving footage supplied with the website.</figcaption></figure></section><details class="studio-fold"><summary>24 names to begin exploring the region</summary><section class="guide-section" id="village-directory"><span class="guide-story-label">The village neighbourhood</span><h2>24 names to begin exploring the region</h2><p>The district publishes separate village-panchayat lists for Pallipet, R.K. Pet and Tiruttani blocks. These selected entries help you identify places by their administrative area. They are a regional directory, not a distance ranking or a list of villages within Podaturpet town limits.</p><div class="village-group"><h3>Pallipet block</h3><ul class="village-list"><li><span lang="en">Athimanjeri</span><span lang="ta">அத்திமாஞ்சேரி</span></li><li><span lang="en">Keechalam</span><span lang="ta">கீச்சலம்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Kolathur</span><span lang="ta">கொளத்தூர்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Nediyam</span><span lang="ta">நெடியம்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Nochili</span><span lang="ta">நொச்சிலி</span></li><li><span lang="en">Pandravedu</span><span lang="ta">பாண்டரவேடு</span></li><li><span lang="en">Punniyam</span><span lang="ta">புண்ணியம்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Veliagaram</span><span lang="ta">வெளியகரம்</span></li></ul><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://cdn.s3waas.gov.in/s39431c87f273e507e6040fcb07dcb4509/uploads/2018/05/2018051595.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pallipet village panchayats (PDF) ↗</a></p></div><div class="village-group"><h3>R.K. Pet block</h3><ul class="village-list"><li><span lang="en">Ammaiyarkuppam</span><span lang="ta">அம்மையார்குப்பம்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Ammanneri</span><span lang="ta">அம்மனேரி</span></li><li><span lang="en">Aswarevanthapuram</span><span lang="ta">அஸ்வரேவந்தபுரம்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Balapuram</span><span lang="ta">பாலாபுரம்</span></li><li><span lang="en">R.K.Pet</span><span lang="ta">ஆர்.கே.பேட்டை</span></li><li><span lang="en">Vanganoor</span><span lang="ta">வங்கனூர்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Vediyangadu</span><span lang="ta">வெடியங்காடு</span></li><li><span lang="en">Vellathur</span><span lang="ta">வெள்ளாத்தூர்</span></li></ul><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://cdn.s3waas.gov.in/s39431c87f273e507e6040fcb07dcb4509/uploads/2018/05/2018051588.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">R.K. Pet village panchayats (PDF) ↗</a></p></div><div class="village-group"><h3>Tiruttani block</h3><ul class="village-list"><li><span lang="en">Agoor</span><span lang="ta">அகூர்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Cherukkanur</span><span lang="ta">செருக்கனூர்</span></li><li><span lang="en">K.G. Kandigai</span><span lang="ta">கே.ஜி.கண்டிகை</span></li><li><span lang="en">Maddur</span><span lang="ta">மத்தூர்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Murukkampattu</span><span lang="ta">முருக்கம்பட்டு</span></li><li><span lang="en">Suryanagaram</span><span lang="ta">சூரியநகரம்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Thadur</span><span lang="ta">தாழூர்</span></li><li><span lang="en">Velancheri</span><span lang="ta">வேலஞ்சேரி</span></li></ul><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://cdn.s3waas.gov.in/s39431c87f273e507e6040fcb07dcb4509/uploads/2018/05/2018051541.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruttani village panchayats (PDF) ↗</a></p></div><p>English spellings follow the district PDFs, uploaded in 2018 and linked from its development page. Local signs may use different spellings. Use the block name with the village name when looking up a place or asking for directions.</p><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://tiruvallur.nic.in/administrative-setup/development/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruvallur District: development blocks ↗</a></p></section></details><article class="guide-story studio-story" id="festival-story"><h2>Amman festivals and the town’s shared calendar</h2><p>The town profile lists an Amman festival lasting seven days in September and identifies Pooniyamman temple on Ponniyamman Koil Street. This gives the town story a specific local landmark and a festival tradition to explore.</p><p>Treat that month as a description in the published profile, not a confirmed calendar for this year. Ask the temple or local organisers for the actual dates and programme before arranging a visit.</p><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://townpanchayat.in/podhaturpet/town_profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Podhaturpet Town Panchayat: town profile and festivals ↗</a></p></article><article class="guide-story studio-story" id="district-story"><h2>Reading the town within Tiruvallur’s history</h2><p>Tiruvallur district’s history records its formation through the division of the former Chengalpattu district. Its account includes the Tiruttani area and Pallipattu sub-taluk among the territories brought together. This helps explain why local history appears under more than one administrative name in older records.</p><p>District history provides a regional frame. A date associated with a dynasty, temple or neighbouring town should not automatically become Podaturpet’s founding date.</p><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://tiruvallur.nic.in/about-district/history/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruvallur District: history ↗</a></p></article><section class="guide-section" id="regional-stories"><span class="guide-story-label">Beyond the town</span><h2>Temple hills and Andhra connections</h2><p>These are wider regional connections, separate from the village directory above. For practical sightseeing information, use our places-to-visit guide.</p></section><article class="guide-story studio-story" id="tiruttani-story"><h2>Tiruttani: a hill, 365 steps and devotional song</h2><p>Tiruttani’s Murugan temple is one of the six Arupadai Veedu shrines. The district’s account describes its 365 steps and the December 31 step festival, when devotees ascend with Tiruppugazh singing. It also identifies Aadi Krittikai as a major celebration.</p><p>This is a story of poetry and worship as well as a hilltop landmark. The district connects the shrine with Arunagirinathar’s devotional work. Festival access and arrangements should be checked with the temple when planning a visit.</p><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://tiruvallur.nic.in/tourist-place/lord-arulmigu-subramaniya-swami-temple-tiruttani/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruvallur District: Tiruttani Murugan temple ↗</a></p></article><article class="guide-story studio-story" id="nagari-story"><h2>Nagari and Tiruttani: names on the town’s regional map</h2><p>The Podhaturpet town profile names Nagari and Tiruttani in its surrounding-town information and identifies Tiruttani as its nearest railway station. Those names are useful starting points for understanding the town’s connections on either side of the Tamil Nadu–Andhra Pradesh area.</p><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://townpanchayat.in/podhaturpet/town_profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Podhaturpet Town Panchayat: town profile and festivals ↗</a></p></article><article class="guide-story studio-story" id="kailasakona-story"><h2>Kailasakona: a waterfall in the wider landscape</h2><p>Across in Andhra Pradesh, the Ministry of Tourism places Kailasakona waterfall in Narayanavanam mandal, Tirupati district. It describes a Shiva–Parvathi temple near the falls and locates the approach along the Uthukkottai–Puttur–Tirupati road.</p><p>The setting adds a nature chapter to a region often introduced through temples and textiles. It is a separate regional excursion, not a village inside Podaturpet. Check current access and weather before travelling.</p><p class="story-citation"><a href="https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/andhra-pradesh/tirupati/kailasakona-waterfall" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ministry of Tourism: Kailasakona waterfall ↗</a></p></article><details class="studio-fold"><summary>Explore the sources</summary><section class="guide-section" id="story-sources"><h2>Explore the sources</h2><p>Researched and updated on 10 September 2026. These public records support the town facts, village groupings and regional stories above. The village PDFs establish administrative listings; they do not establish individual village founding dates or every village’s weaving history.</p><ol class="guide-source-list"><li><a href="https://townpanchayat.in/podhaturpet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Podhaturpet Town Panchayat: general profile</a></li><li><a href="https://townpanchayat.in/podhaturpet/town_profile" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Podhaturpet Town Panchayat: town profile and festivals</a></li><li><a href="https://tiruvallur.nic.in/about-district/history/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruvallur District: history</a></li><li><a href="https://tiruvallur.nic.in/administrative-setup/development/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruvallur District: development blocks</a></li><li><a href="https://cdn.s3waas.gov.in/s39431c87f273e507e6040fcb07dcb4509/uploads/2018/05/2018051595.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pallipet village panchayats (PDF)</a></li><li><a href="https://cdn.s3waas.gov.in/s39431c87f273e507e6040fcb07dcb4509/uploads/2018/05/2018051588.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">R.K. Pet village panchayats (PDF)</a></li><li><a href="https://cdn.s3waas.gov.in/s39431c87f273e507e6040fcb07dcb4509/uploads/2018/05/2018051541.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruttani village panchayats (PDF)</a></li><li><a href="https://tiruvallur.nic.in/tourist-place/lord-arulmigu-subramaniya-swami-temple-tiruttani/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tiruvallur District: Tiruttani Murugan temple</a></li><li><a href="https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/andhra-pradesh/tirupati/kailasakona-waterfall" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ministry of Tourism: Kailasakona waterfall</a></li></ol></section></details><aside class="story-next"><h2>Keep exploring Podaturpet</h2><div><a href="/podaturpet-tourist-places.html">Plan places to visit</a><a href="/podaturpet-lungi-weaving-story.html">Read the lungi weaving story</a><a href="/lungi-product-catalogue.html">Explore lungi designs</a></div></aside><section class="guide-directory-cta"><h2>Does your village have a story to share?</h2><p>Tell us the village name, the event or memory, and when it happened. Original photographs, dated records and first-hand accounts can help bring the next chapter to life. Send only material you have permission to share.</p><a href="https://wa.me/14793201970?text=Hello%20Podaturpet%20Team%2C%20I%20would%20like%20to%20share%20a%20village%20story." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Share a village story</a></section></div></div><section class="pt-feature" id="community-stories"><h2>Help tell the next Podaturpet story.</h2><div class="pt-grid"><article class="pt-card"><h3>A day in Podaturpet</h3><p>Share original photographs of familiar streets, shops, fields and everyday life. Tell us where and when each picture was taken.</p><a href="/podaturpet-town-guide.html?contribute=photo#contribute">Share your town photos</a></article><article class="pt-card"><h3>Meet the weavers</h3><p>What did you learn first? What makes a good weave? Share a short interview with the weaver’s permission.</p><a href="/podaturpet-town-guide.html?contribute=story#contribute">Contribute a weaver’s story</a></article><article class="pt-card"><h3>Then and now</h3><p>Have an old photograph and a current view of the same place? Share both with dates, credits and permission.</p><a href="/podaturpet-town-guide.html?contribute=photo#contribute">Share a town memory</a></article></div></section></main>
